{
  "title": "The Ultimate Collection",
  "artist": "Sade",
  "year": 2011,
  "release_date": "2011-05-09",
  "type": "Album + Compilation",
  "description": "The Ultimate Collection is the second greatest hits album by English band Sade, released on 29 April 2011 by RCA Records. The album includes several singles from the band's career, including \"Your Love Is King\", \"Smooth Operator\", \"By Your Side\", \"No Ordinary Love\" and \"Soldier of Love\". It also contains four previously unreleased tracks—a cover of Thin Lizzy's 1974 song \"Still in Love with You\", a remix of \"The Moon and the Sky\" featuring Jay-Z, and the songs \"I Would Never Have Guessed\" and \"Love Is Found\". The band promoted the album with their first concert tour in 10 years, Sade Live. In March 2014, the album was re-released as The Essential Sade under the Sony Legacy umbrella.",
